{"path":"3/library/getpass.html","title":"getpass — Portable password input","description":"Source code: Lib/getpass.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-getpass"},{"type":"anchor","id":"getpass-portable-password-input"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"getpass"},{"type":"text","value":" — Portable password input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/getpass.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/getpass.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"3/library/intro.html#availability","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Availability"}]},{"type":"text","value":": not WASI."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module does not work or is not available on WebAssembly. See "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/intro.html#wasm-availability","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebAssembly platforms"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"getpass"},{"type":"text","value":" module provides two functions:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"getpass.getpass","term":[{"type":"text","value":"getpass.getpass("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"'Password: "},{"type":"text","value":"'"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"*"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prompt the user for a password without echoing. The user is prompted using the string "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which defaults to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Password: '"},{"type":"text","value":". On Unix, the prompt is written to the file-like object "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream"}]},{"type":"text","value":" using the replace error handler if needed. "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream"}]},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to the controlling terminal ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/dev/tty"},{"type":"text","value":") or if that is unavailable to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.stderr"},{"type":"text","value":" (this argument is ignored on Windows)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument controls how user input is displayed while typing. If "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":" (default), input remains hidden. Otherwise, "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"}]},{"type":"text","value":" must be a single printable ASCII character and each typed character is replaced by it. For example, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"echo_char='*'"},{"type":"text","value":" will display asterisks instead of the actual input."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If echo free input is unavailable getpass() falls back to printing a warning message to "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stream"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and reading from "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.stdin"},{"type":"text","value":" and issuing a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/getpass.html#getpass.GetPassWarning","title":"getpass.GetPassWarning","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"GetPassWarning"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you call getpass from within IDLE, the input may be done in the terminal you launched IDLE from rather than the idle window itself."}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Unix systems, when "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is set, the terminal will be configured to operate in "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://manpages.debian.org/termios(3)#Canonical_and_noncanonical_mode","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"noncanonical mode"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":". In particular, this means that line editing shortcuts such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ctrl"},{"type":"text","value":"+"},{"type":"inline_code","code":"U"},{"type":"text","value":" will not work and may insert unexpected characters into the input."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.14: Added the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"echo_char"}]},{"type":"text","value":" parameter for keyboard feedback."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"getpass.GetPassWarning","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"exception"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"getpass.GetPassWarning"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#UserWarning","title":"UserWarning","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"UserWarning"}]},{"type":"text","value":" subclass issued when password input may be echoed."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"getpass.getuser","term":[{"type":"text","value":"getpass.getuser()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return the “login name” of the user."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function checks the environment variables "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-0"},{"type":"inline_code","code":"LOGNAME"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-1"},{"type":"inline_code","code":"USER"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"LNAME"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-2"},{"type":"inline_code","code":"USERNAME"},{"type":"text","value":", in order, and returns the value of the first one which is set to a non-empty string. If none are set, the login name from the password database is returned on systems which support the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/pwd.html#module-pwd","title":"pwd: The password database (getpwnam() and friends).","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"pwd"}]},{"type":"text","value":" module, otherwise, an "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#OSError","title":"OSError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"OSError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is raised."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In general, this function should be preferred over "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/os.html#os.getlogin","title":"os.getlogin","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"os.getlogin()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.13: Previously, various exceptions beyond just "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#OSError","title":"OSError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"OSError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" were raised."}]}]}]}]}}
